            <ArticleTitle>Characteristics associated with depression in long-term care residents with dementia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the prevalence, assessment, and treatment of, as well as characteristics associated with, depression in residential care/assisted living and nursing home residents with dementia. Overall, 25% of the participants were depressed. Depression was related to severe cognitive impairment, behavioral symptoms, pain, and for-profit nursing home residence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
